WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.370
My first anatomy lesson was not a drawing. A fox lay

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:08.190
on the table. I wanted to understand how its parts worked together.

00:00:09.592 --> 00:00:13.328
Later, I brought a microscope from Cairo to Qatar. At

00:00:13.328 --> 00:00:17.064
home, curiosity did not have to wait for laboratory hours.

00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:22.689
We began with plant extracts and questions about medicinal chemistry.

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:26.911
Some experiments were simple. The answers were rarely as simple.

00:00:28.383 --> 00:00:32.532
Imine synthesis and molecular sensing taught me to distrust

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:36.681
a beautiful explanation until I could interrogate the spectrum.

00:00:38.175 --> 00:00:42.513
We built a student chemistry community. Science grew in shared

00:00:42.513 --> 00:00:46.851
laboratories, long arguments, and the people who challenged our assumptions.

00:00:48.342 --> 00:00:51.916
A polymer would not behave as planned. I learned how

00:00:51.916 --> 00:00:55.490
little a plausible structure tells us about a real material.

00:00:56.883 --> 00:01:01.064
Then I began following developing vessels in zebrafish. The

00:01:01.064 --> 00:01:05.244
organism moved, blood flowed, and measurement became a different problem.

00:01:06.675 --> 00:01:11.331
An embedding attempt failed when agarose and paraffin would not hold

00:01:11.331 --> 00:01:15.988
together. The microtome exposed a materials problem, not a usable section.

00:01:17.467 --> 00:01:20.989
In the lung, we studied what happens when an

00:01:20.989 --> 00:01:24.512
airway reopens and a moving interface injures epithelial cells.

00:01:25.883 --> 00:01:31.010
Biomaterials and engineered surfaces added another constraint: a substance can

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:36.137
be chemically interesting yet behave very differently at an interface.

00:01:37.675 --> 00:01:42.655
Now I study dexamethasone vesicles intended for inhalation. A carrier

00:01:42.655 --> 00:01:47.636
must withstand nebulization before it can even be assessed for delivery.

00:01:49.133 --> 00:01:54.088
I also study how earlier pharmacists made medicines dependable. Across centuries

00:01:54.088 --> 00:01:59.042
and disciplines, I keep returning to what the evidence can actually bear.
